title: Demo
---
This sample shows off using Text Animator in Yarn Spinner with full action markup and Text Animator effect support.
This line has [rainb w=3]a Text Animator effect and a Yarn Spinner pause action [pause=1000 /]done through YS markup.[/rainb] Pretty cool.
Existing [i]Replacement Yarn Markup[/i] also works fine.
As does normal <rainb w=3>Text Animator</rainb> tags.

But the advice is to represent Text Animator tags via Yarn Spinner markup.
You can even do [wave a=3 type=appearance]appearances[/wave] just fine.
The Yarn markup form of the effects is translated into Text Animator tags automatically for you.

Alternatively do it all via Text Animator actions and effects.

We [rainb w=3][bounce]hope[/bounce] you [dangle]Have[/dangle] [/rainb][shake]fun[/shake][rot]![/rot]
===
